Z||000000||SloPonti||02-01-2000||12:24 AM||||does anyone have this for the four cylinder! if so how does it work and what actactly did you buy! how much and how hard to install!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-01-2000||08:24 AM||||MSD 6AL paired with a Crane PS92 coil would do wonders for your car. MSD along with Accel and Blue Streak make decent Ignition control modules (in distributor cap) for the V6 I'm not sure about the 4 though. BUT the MSD box and a nice coil would up the HP, and Torque through out the entire power band, along with uping the fuel milage and reliability. Why a 6AL in stead of a 6A or a Crane Hi-6s (I have a Crane HI-6S and a PS92 with MSD ICM) The 6AL has MUCH more expandability (RPM switches for water injection, nitrous, electric intake ducts... etc.) And with a 6AL you can just unplug it and change to a BTM with out any wiring problems when you ad either a supercharger or a turbo. MSD makes a sweet ignition system but a WEAK coil pack. the Accel super coil I had was ok but once I put on the Crane PS92 I gained 2hp and 3lb-ft at the wheels! they both have a web site if you'd like to get more information about them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||02-01-2000||03:48 PM||||Hope you dont mind me adding my .02...<P>I would not advise using an MSD 6 series ignition with the crane PS-92 coil!  The systems are not compatible(ie.. the coil design determines the driver requirements).  Crane even warns against this combination on their web site:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cranecams.com/ignition1/ps92ps93.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cranecams.com/ignition1/ps92ps93.htm</A> <P>The MSD 6AL has a built-in rev limiter, but it is exactly the same as the 6A in all other aspects(I have owned both).  Either one will work fine with various MSD 6 series timing control units (ie. BTM, etc..), and rpm switches.<P>On the early Fiero 4cyl, the choice for a multi-spark ignition system would be similar to the V6.  The "DIS" ignition is used on later model year L4's, therefore the MSD Digital DIS-2 Ignition (Part #6211), and DIS-2 HO Coil Packs (Part #62111) are specific for this application.<P>Without trying to address the issue of "best coil" directly, consider that nearly all of these aftermarket coils have outputs greater than 40,000 volts. That is more than adequate "for our little V6's", and I highly doubt that more energy than this is going to make much of a difference.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fotofrank||02-01-2000||03:52 PM||||I have an MSD6A and blaster coil on my '84 SE. I'm not so sure that the car has much more poop, but driving at speed and lifting my foot off the accelerator and the car does not slow down . Before the MSD6A the car whold noticable slow( RPM drop and felt like a down shift) when my foot came off the accelerator while driving at about 35 MPH. The net thing will be a Holley TBI.<BR>P.S. My car is an automatic with 116000 miles on it.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Cooter||02-01-2000||04:11 PM||||I have the MSD 6AL and MSD's HEI coil. I also got the MSD adapter harness so everything just plugs in. I really don't know how much it helped power or economy, but I get about 30 MPG and do not have any problems accelerating or passing any more.||||reg||1
